    "headline": "Cold enough to hold methane gas",
    "detail": "Methane survives only in atmospheres below roughly 1,300 K, cooler than any true star. It absorbs light near 3.3 \u00b5m, which is why this object is 2.4\u00d7 brighter at 4\u20134.75 \u00b5m.",
